Type **/** in the search bar to try one. A slash command opens a menu in the composer, and picking an item runs its `execute` callback:

```tsx
const slash = unstable_useSlashCommandAdapter({
  commands: [{ id: "library", execute: () => showLibrary() }],
  removeOnExecute: true,
});

<ComposerTriggerPopover char="/" {...slash} />
```

Mentions use the same trigger popover, with **@** in place of **/**.
